blossom reuses code from the following open-source projects. Original
copyright headers are kept on every copied file, and modified files carry a
"Modified for blossom, <year>." line below that header.

- BitChord — https://github.com/kushagrasinghx/BitChord — GPL-3.0
  Tag v1.9.1, commit 7f45c768a461fd7e68bf4613f71e8a767e643d4c.
  Taken: the YouTube Music Innertube client, its parser and stream resolution
  (source/youtubemusic); the lyrics providers and the LRC/enhanced LRC/TTML
  parsers (feature/lyrics); Spotify public-playlist and library reading
  (source/spotify); the Last.fm and ListenBrainz clients (feature/integrations).

- Spotube — https://github.com/KRTirtho/spotube — AGPL-3.0-or-later
  Tag v6.0.0, commit 8925b1b9351c3af2fd672db898d8d899badc1cb9.
  Taken: the libVLC (vlcj) desktop audio engine and its VLC bundling setup
  (core/player, composeApp packaging); the system media control service for
  Linux MPRIS and Windows SMTC (core/player).

Libraries used as dependencies (not copied), with their licenses:
- InnerTubeX (MetrolistGroup/innertubex) — GPL-3.0
- NewPipe Extractor (TeamNewPipe/NewPipeExtractor) — GPL-3.0
- vlcj (caprica/vlcj) — GPL-3.0; libVLC (VideoLAN) — LGPL-2.1-or-later
- Nucleus media-control (NucleusFramework/Nucleus) — MIT
- The full list is generated from the dependency graph and shown in the app
  under Settings → About → Open-source licenses.

